        "original_id": "c0ba763a-d101-5b87-83b5-d00cfb2c6711",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Donna Mills, Clint Eastwood, Florence Henderson, Pam Grier, Ken Watanabe, Kazunari Ninomiya\n- Works: Love Is a Many Splendored Thing, Play Misty for Me, Ladies of the House, Letters from Iwo Jima\n- Roles: Tobie Williams\n- Topics: film and television acting, directing\n\nFacts:\n- Donna Mills starred for three years in the soap opera Love Is a Many Splendored Thing from 1967 to 1970.\n- In 1971, Donna Mills starred as Tobie Williams, the girlfriend of Clint Eastwood's character, in the cult film Play Misty for Me.\n- Play Misty for Me is a 1971 American psychological thriller film directed by and starring Clint Eastwood in his directorial debut.\n- Ladies of the House stars Florence Henderson, Donna Mills, and Pam Grier.\n- Letters from Iwo Jima is a 2006 Japanese-American war film directed and co-produced by Clint Eastwood and starring Ken Watanabe and Kazunari Ninomiya.",
